## Roles

The pipeline uses role templates to define agent behavior. Default roles are active out of the box. Additional roles can be instantiated from built-in templates.

### Active Roles

| Role | Stages | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| planner | planning | Scope, design, file targeting |
| implementer | implementing, fixing | Write code, run tests, fix issues |
| reviewer | reviewing | Validate, test, produce reports |
| researcher | researching | Extract patterns, update knowledge |

### Available Templates

Additional roles can be activated with `/init-roles`:

| Template | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| lead | Pipeline orchestration (active by default via hooks) |
| coder | Alternative implementer for feature coding |
| code-reviewer | Code-focused review (style, patterns, best practices) |
| designer | System and architecture design |
| ux-designer | UX/UI design |
| qa-tester | QA testing and test coverage |
| devops | Infrastructure, CI/CD, deployment |

### Customizing Roles

Role instances live in `.agent/roles/`. Override any template field:

```yaml
# .agent/roles/implementer.md
---
model: opus              # override default model
skills:
  - testing
  - react-patterns       # project-specific skill
knowledge:
  - patterns
  - conventions
pipeline_stages: [implementing, fixing]
---
```

